---
---
<section class="section" id="pathway">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">04 · Agent Development Pathway</span>
      <h2>From design to internal experimentation to production publishing</h2>
      <p>
        Teams build new AKD agents through a stage-gated pathway that moves from design to
        internal experimentation to production publishing. The pathway is intentionally
        separated into two product surfaces — AKD Labs for everything before an agent is
        ready, and AKD Flow for everything after — with an SME-led review gate in between.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="pathway-services" aria-label="AKD services available to teams">
      <div class="services-head">
        <span class="services-eyebrow">AKD services teams can use</span>
        <p>
          Governance and safety services come built in — available across every stage of the pathway. Teams pick what they need; the list below is a non-exhaustive sample, not an ordered priority.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="services-list">
        <li>
          <b>Reusable Scientific Tools</b>
          <span>MCP-wrapped search, retrieval, and analysis tools that agents compose instead of re-implementing.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>FactReasoner</b>
          <span>Targeted factuality reasoning over claims, attribution, and supporting evidence to mitigate hallucinations.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Risk Agent</b>
          <span>An LLM judge that evaluates outputs against the IBM Risk Atlas and a NASA Science Literature Risk taxonomy, along with context-specific risks for each agent.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Compliance Checking</b>
          <span>Automated guardrail layer enforcing science-specific constraints on inputs and outputs.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Science Guardrails</b>
          <span>A reusable input/output safety net — each guardrail acts as a checkpoint between an AI agent and the outside world.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Granite Guardian</b>
          <span>A fast, content-focused moderation LLM based on the IBM Granite family — assesses jailbreaks, harm, bias, plus RAG-specific groundedness checks.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </aside>

    <div class="pathway-diagram" aria-label="Agent development pathways">

      <!-- Row 0: Common start -->
      <div class="pathway-row pathway-row--start">
        <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--featured">
          <span>Phase 1 · All Agents</span>
          <b>Design (CARE methodology)</b>
          <p class="pipe-desc">
            Teams start with the AKD CARE process. Subject matter experts, developers, and
            helper LLM agents work through five phases — scope, key information elicitation,
            reasoning policy and guardrails, implementation, benchmarking — passing a stage
            gate at each phase. The output is a set of reusable design artifacts that will
            later become operational code.
          </p>
          <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> CARE phase gates — joint SME / developer / agent approval at each phase</p>
          <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/akd-care" target="_blank" rel="noopener">akd-care ↗</a>
        </div>
        <div class="fork-indicator" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="fork-line fork-line--left"></span>
          <span class="fork-node">↓ choose path</span>
          <span class="fork-line fork-line--right"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Row 1: Two branches -->
      <div class="pathway-row pathway-row--branches">

        <!-- Branch A: Simple Agents -->
        <div class="branch branch--simple">
          <div class="branch-label">Tool-Independent</div>
          <div class="pipe-step">
            <span>Phase 2a · Simple Agents</span>
            <b>Custom GPT</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Simple Agents are tool-independent AI agents designed through the AKD CARE
              process — no custom APIs, MCP servers, or external integrations required.
              Paste the CARE-developed prompt as GPT instructions, upload domain context,
              and select the recommended model. Examples: Scientific Illustrator,
              Paper Writing Assistant, NASA Data Governance.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> Public-use policy approval; baseline guardrail prompt patterns embedded by CARE</p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/agents" target="_blank" rel="noopener">agents/ ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Branch B: Tool-Integrated Agents -->
        <div class="branch branch--tool">
          <div class="branch-label">Tool-Integrated</div>
          <div class="pipe-step">
            <span>Phase 2b · Tool-Integrated Agents</span>
            <b>Build in akd-ext</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              More complex agents require external tools, APIs, or data systems for
              execution along with rigorous prompt design and reasoning. Implement the
              agent in akd-ext: author tool wrappers, MCP integrations, and API clients.
              Examples: Earth Science Data Search (CMR), Code Search, Astro Data Search.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> Tools whitelist; static MCP-server config; guardrail integration required</p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/akd-ext" target="_blank" rel="noopener">akd-ext ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
          <div class="pipe-step">
            <span>Phase 3b</span>
            <b>Build and benchmark in AKD Labs</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Teams import the CARE artifacts into AKD Labs and begin to iterate. Author
              the system prompt and tool configuration, chat-test the agent in the Chat
              Lab, inspect full trace logs (system prompt, tool inputs and outputs,
              reasoning summary, token usage, estimated cost), and run benchmarks against
              a prepared test suite. AKD Labs is multi-tenant and scoped to a project or
              organization, but experimental agents stay internal to the team that owns them.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> Internal-only scope; benchmark thresholds enforced before review</p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://labs.akd.odsi.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">labs.akd.odsi.io ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--gov-gate">
            <span>Phase 4b</span>
            <b>Readiness review</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              When the agent meets its design requirements, an SME lead conducts a
              readiness review. The agent must demonstrate scientific integrity
              (non-prescriptive behavior, traceable reasoning), guardrail compliance, and
              benchmark results before promotion is approved. This is the moment the team
              commits to publishing the agent for users beyond the project.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag gov-tag--strong"><span>Governance:</span> This stage <em>is</em> the gate — no agent reaches Flow without SME sign-off</p>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
          <div class="pipe-step">
            <span>Phase 5b</span>
            <b>Publish to AKD Flow</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Approved agents are published to AKD Flow and to the akd-ext code
              repository. Once an agent is in AKD Flow, scientists can compose it into
              multi-agent workflows through the natural language planner, run those
              workflows with streaming updates and guardrail badges, and share results.
            </p>
            <p class="gov-tag"><span>Governance:</span> Operational guardrails active in production; HITL checkpoints in every workflow run</p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://flow.akd.odsi.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">flow.akd.odsi.io ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Row 2: Distribution endpoints -->
      <div class="pathway-row pathway-row--end">
        <div class="merge-indicator" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="fork-line fork-line--left"></span>
          <span class="fork-node">↓ distribute</span>
          <span class="fork-line fork-line--right"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="endpoints-grid">
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--endpoint">
            <span class="endpoint-tag">Endpoint</span>
            <b>AKD Flow Workflows</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Composed multi-agent pipelines on the AKD Flow canvas — scientists
              assemble approved agents, run workflows with streaming updates and
              guardrail badges, and share reproducible results.
            </p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://flow.akd.odsi.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">flow.akd.odsi.io ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--endpoint">
            <span class="endpoint-tag">Endpoint</span>
            <b>Custom GPT Directory</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Tool-independent agents published directly as Custom GPTs using the
              CARE-developed system prompt — no custom code required. Examples:
              Scientific Illustrator, Paper Writing Assistant, Data Governance Agent.
            </p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/agents" target="_blank" rel="noopener">agents/ ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--endpoint">
            <span class="endpoint-tag">Endpoint</span>
            <b>Community MCP Servers</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Teams hosting their own MCP servers with agents that integrate via the
              AKD framework. Community-contributed agents are governed by the same
              CARE and SME-review process as first-party agents.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pipe-step pipe-step--endpoint">
            <span class="endpoint-tag">Endpoint</span>
            <b>akd-ext Open-Source Repo</b>
            <p class="pipe-desc">
              Published agent code on GitHub — available for forking, peer review,
              and integration into other projects. The canonical reference for
              tool-integrated domain agents across the AKD ecosystem.
            </p>
            <a class="pipe-link" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd-suite/tree/main/akd-ext" target="_blank" rel="noopener">akd-ext ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* ---- AKD services panel (above the pathway) ---- */
  .pathway-services {
    margin-top: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 22px 24px 24px;
    background: var(--bg-0);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  }
  .services-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .services-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .services-head p {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .services-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .services-list li {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 12px 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .services-list b {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .services-list span {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .services-list { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .services-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* ---- Layout skeleton ---- */
  .pathway-diagram {
    margin-top: 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
  }

  /* Start row: full-width featured card */
  .pathway-row--start,
  .pathway-row--end {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .pathway-row--start .pipe-step,
  .pathway-row--end .pipe-step {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  /* Branch row: two columns */
  .pathway-row--branches {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* Branch column */
  .branch {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0;
  }

  /* Branch label tag */
  .branch-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  /* Arrow between cards in a branch */
  .branch-arrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1;
    padding: 6px 0;
  }

  /* ---- Fork / merge indicators ---- */
  .fork-indicator,
  .merge-indicator {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 12px 0;
    gap: 0;
  }
  .fork-line {
    flex: 1;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .fork-node {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding: 0 12px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* ---- Card: pipe-step ---- */
  .pipe-step {
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 22px 18px;
    background: var(--bg-0);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
    text-align: left;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* Featured (start / end) card gets a subtle accent top border */
  .pipe-step--featured {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.05), 0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);
  }
  .pipe-step--featured::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 2px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0 0;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--accent), transparent);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .pipe-step b {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 17px;
    display: block;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .pipe-step span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .pipe-desc {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .pipe-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid oklch(0.546 0.245 262.881 / 0.35);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    margin-top: 4px;
    align-self: flex-start;
    transition: border-bottom-color 0.18s ease, color 0.18s ease;
  }

  /* ---- Governance tag inside each pipe-step ---- */
  .gov-tag {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    background: oklch(0.97 0.005 262.881);
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .gov-tag span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-right: 4px;
  }
  .gov-tag--strong {
    border-left-width: 4px;
    background: oklch(0.95 0.012 262.881);
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .pipe-step--gov-gate {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .pipe-link:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent-4);
  }

  /* ---- Distribution endpoints grid ---- */
  .endpoints-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .pipe-step--endpoint {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .pipe-step--endpoint::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 2px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0 0;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--accent), transparent);
    opacity: 0.4;
  }

  .endpoint-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* ---- Responsive ---- */
  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .endpoints-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .pathway-row--branches {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .pathway-row--start .pipe-step,
    .pathway-row--end .pipe-step {
      max-width: 100%;
    }
    .fork-indicator,
    .merge-indicator {
      max-width: 100%;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 580px) {
    .endpoints-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
